+## Context
+
+Task #2356 builds on accepted B1/B2, backend master 083d45cc264f458d8399aeb7d18ec8b2c29d8daa. The dedicated read-only frontend mirror is c98e6b7c834e876b167ec41afdb4a7323d63ad0f. Exact F1 schema5/recipe3/descriptor3 interface compatibility passes, but bounded restartable planning and persisted measured PDF pages are missing; #2354 is active again. See proposal.md for user motivation.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+Produce a single complete certified file without memory growing with the archive. Use the owner's explicitly approved isolated PDF profile (2026-10-10): up to1GiB RAM and128 processes/threads, unchanged CPU.25 and concurrency one. Preserve every other explicit portion/profile threshold across Python, Node, browser, decoder and composer descendants. B2's existing256MiB/64pid defaults remain compatible; the new profile is an explicit opt-in and requires new matching capacity evidence. No synthetic total-count restriction, hidden budget increase or alternate template renderer.
+
+## Decisions
+
+1. Canonical F1 ports. Require a versioned bounded plan-step with checksummed private checkpoint references and exact measured-PDF output. Persist tokenizer/writer/context/UTF8/record offsets through an owned, licensed vendor-derived public checkpoint port with exact semantic/decode-table pins and disk-backed foreign context. Public open-stack reconstruction was independently disproved by the executed <svg><foreignobject></svg> control (changed close-callback ordering); it is rejected. Never serialize undocumented upstream private fields or replay an entire huge field as one portion. Indexing, anchor discovery, planning, front matter and coverage each have bounded cursors. A portable incremental canonical hash state or bounded replay must retain B1's exact hash, not substitute a Merkle digest. F1 public DTO/source5 replay remains compatible; the additive artifact receives a new content pin. Reject a second Python renderer and whole diagnostic runWorker integration.
+
+2. Lifecycle and writes. book_exports owns every job/checkpoint write. BookJobLifecycleService claims render with the existing global slot/lease/epoch; a rendering service supervises exact artifact/runtime identity and bounded subprocesses. BookRenderPublicationService verifies ordered immutable outputs and independently fenced receipts. Views only validate/authorize and delegate. Private files use owned attempt paths, 0700 directories, 0600 exclusive writes, checksums and atomic publication; crash orphans are reclaimed by existing cleanup. Database checkpoints stay <=4096 bytes; growing ledgers/cursors reside on private disk. No migration, cross-app model writes or async-schema changes are planned.
+
+3. Exact page bytes. The F1 physical adapter persists the exact successful one-A4 <=4 MiB measurement output after layout/resource/coverage checks, with checksum/length/pages in the immutable receipt. B3 does not reopen arbitrary saved HTML in another browser/network. Original media, printed derivatives, encoder/fonts and settings/snapshot hashes are independently bound to the receipt.
+
+4. Composition. Measure body/atlas, then front matter/TOC and final global folios. Use file-based bounded/hierarchical composition with a segment ledger, explicit page destinations/bookmarks/labels and document metadata. Verify final counts/source coverage and destinations before certificate publication. Candidate qpdf/runtime commands are pinned and must pass real same-profile composer spikes before adoption; a giant in-memory PDF library or unchecked concat is rejected. Complete-file verification advances bounded chunks; current whole-snapshot publication verification must not become an unbounded final portion.
+
+5. Delivery. A book_exports ticket service uses a short-lived purpose-separated signed payload bound to job, owner, immutable artifact checksum and expiry. Download-ticket POST requires normal owner authentication, an empty body and a complete retained certificate. Ticket GET uses only that purpose-specific authority; repeated/unknown parameters and mismatched jobs fail closed. Current owner/source ACL is checked before and throughout existing bounded streaming. Cancellation/expiry/revocation invalidates authority without a persistent account token. Response URLs stay same-origin; private no-store/no-referrer and checksum headers are mandatory. Existing authenticated download remains additive compatible.
+
+6. Readiness. Preserve B2 snapshot readiness separately; B3 capability requires renderer+Linux executable/font/composer identity and full render/merge/verify measurements for actual1000/5000 workloads with an external numerical app-health observer. The Linux ARM64 feasibility container is development evidence only. No readiness or capability switch precedes exact production AMD64 proof. Cache aliases are unchanged and no persistent ticket cache is introduced.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- [Python + Node + Chromium may exceed256MiB] -> isolated exact-runtime spike before integrating, preserve hard cap, report real failure instead of raising limits.
+- [Parser restart changes malformed HTML semantics] -> owned explicit typed public checkpoint API, disk-backed hidden foreign stack and bounded directly-addressed source spool, with unchanged licensed vendor semantics; uninterrupted/restarted/chunk-size fragment/text/media parity including ghost namespace context, entities/rawtext/implicit closes, table/list/FAQ and UTF8 boundaries. Adjacent text callback subdivision requires identical canonical writer output.
+- [Composer RSS grows with pages] -> same-profile1000/5000 hierarchical merge/destination spike; explicit bounded failure if no valid implementation fits.
+- [Foreign source changes contaminate artifact] -> publish from clean canonical task paths and refresh dedicated mirror only after reviewed commit; exact manifest/file hashes are mandatory.
+- [Cancellation races final publication] -> existing epoch fencing, source ACL and private-storage verification rechecked before short atomic commit.
+
+## Migration Plan
+
+Complete planning and additive F1 ports, review/publish/accept exact artifact, then implement B3 under the existing waiting dependency. Run canonical relevant queued Docker tests plus independent adversarial reviews. Commit explicit task paths on master, push and transition to testing. Use the authorized original-card production cycle and Compose-v2 canonical rollout; deploy worker opt-in with capability false first, capture actual complete-file/resource/ACL evidence, then enable only matching readiness. Keep original card/OpenSpec in testing until deployed revision and all acceptance pass. Rollback to prior reviewed source/runtime and disable B3 capability/worker; retained original snapshot bytes are never rewritten. Sync/archive only after all required evidence exists.
+
+## Feasibility evidence and current hold — 2026-10-10
+
+Two local Linux ARM64 diagnostics fail the unchanged profile before the first page. Django+Node+Chromium reached585461760 summed RSS bytes with a real cgroup OOM kill. Phase-local Node64 without Django reached601870336 summed RSS bytes (Chromium alone460533760) and pids64 exhaustion. The actual ARM64 executable reports149.0.7827.0 despite installer149.0.7827.55, so these are not exact production AMD64 acceptance. Parent frontend ignored reports SHA444644eef1e276cea05090521f2992f170d8edbdd0f28ff6aae0f58858fbfee1 and aa5a6efb85f17a23072193d8b1ea284ab514dc43da1da6931dfcd99d31a333df preserve complete commands/events; no PDF or composer passed. The root has requested an explicit material resource-contract decision (up to1GiB/pids128, CPU.25 unchanged). Until an actual human answer,256MiB/pids64 remain authoritative, no resource configuration is changed, no capability is enabled. Independent canonical checkpoint/PDF persistence work continues.
+
+## Explicit resource decision — 2026-10-10
+
+The owner replied “Да, подготовить новый профиль и проверить” to the exact1GiB/128pids/CPU.25 question. This authorizes preparing and testing that isolated resource envelope, not readiness or production capacity. Existing Compose memory256m and PID64 defaults stay unchanged; BOOK_EXPORT_WORKER_MEMORY_LIMIT=1g and BOOK_EXPORT_WORKER_PIDS_LIMIT=128 select the candidate explicitly. The approved numeric profile must be derived from the existing complete profile with only the authorized memory/PID changes and a new id/hash; missing portion/health/disk thresholds must not be invented. B3 must enforce the PID cgroup bound and all descendant metrics. Actual productionAMD64 runtime identity, full1000/5000 PDF/composition and continuous external app-health still gate readiness.
+
+Source inspection also found that Parser depth is not bounded by Writer depth (uppercaseIMG family). Canonical restart therefore needs an immutable linked disk tag stack with checkpointed lookup/pop/events and staged EOF. Bound work per call; never impose a new total parser-depth cap or change case/void semantics. The public bounded step returns acceptedChars and needsDrain; no new input may overtake pending semantic work.
