+## Purpose
+
+Produce complete canonical travel-book PDFs as durable bounded jobs and deliver verified private files without archive-wide browser memory or lost source content.
+
+## ADDED Requirements
+
+### Requirement: Complete canonical content
+
+The worker SHALL consume a pinned canonical renderer artifact and frozen B1 settings/source order. It MUST preserve every enabled source block and distinct media occurrence, the twenty themes, captions, aspect ratios, disclosure answers and locale formatting. Missing or corrupt resources MUST fail explicitly rather than disappear.
+
+#### Scenario: Luxembourg and complete large archive
+- **WHEN** the selected accessible book contains a long article or 1000/5000 enabled photo placements
+- **THEN** the output contains the complete enabled text and ordered media without a total product count cap or truncated field
+
+#### Scenario: Missing photo or incompatible renderer
+- **WHEN** frozen bytes fail integrity or the actual renderer identity differs from the pinned identity
+- **THEN** the job cannot publish a complete file and reports an explicit retryable or compatibility error
+
+### Requirement: Durable bounded planning and rendering
+
+All planning, physical rendering and composition SHALL advance bounded epoch-fenced checkpoints under the unchanged accepted B2 resource profile. Restart MUST reuse confirmed sources and page PDFs without duplicate source coverage, and stale authority MUST NOT publish progress. Whole-field or whole-book processing as one nominal portion is forbidden.
+
+#### Scenario: Restart within a huge field
+- **WHEN** a worker stops during planning or printing an oversized field and compatible execution resumes
+- **THEN** the final ordered text/media/page coverage equals uninterrupted execution and only confirmed immutable progress is reused
+
+#### Scenario: Budget exhaustion or expired lease
+- **WHEN** a phase exceeds its approved budget or attempts to commit under expired authority
+- **THEN** no false complete checkpoint is committed; divisible work is reduced or an explicit bounded failure preserves earlier progress
+
+### Requirement: Physical complete document certificate
+
+The final private PDF SHALL have actual page counts, global folios, correctly offset TOC destinations/bookmarks/page labels, and pinned document metadata. Publication MUST independently verify complete source and placement coverage, measured page receipts, settings/order/runtime identity, file checksum/length and same-profile readiness.
+
+#### Scenario: Front matter shifts chapter offsets
+- **WHEN** measured front matter spans multiple physical pages
+- **THEN** printed folios and document destinations point to the final correct physical chapter pages
+
+#### Scenario: Partial receipt or incomplete composition
+- **WHEN** a page, placement, resource binding or complete-file checksum is missing or mismatched
+- **THEN** completeness stays incomplete and no download becomes available
+
+### Requirement: Private scoped streamed delivery
+
+An authenticated owner SHALL obtain POST /api/exports/books/{job_id}/download-ticket/ returning download_url and expires_at only for a retained certified file. GET /api/exports/books/{job_id}/download/?ticket=... SHALL authorize a short-lived job/owner/artifact-scoped ticket without exposing an account token. Download MUST stream bounded chunks and enforce current source ACL, owner availability and retention. Responses MUST carry PDF content type, byte length, checksum, private no-store and no-referrer headers.
+
+#### Scenario: Owner downloads after a page reload
+- **WHEN** the owner recovers a completed job and obtains a valid ticket
+- **THEN** the direct download streams the same certified complete file without buffering the whole PDF in browser memory
+
+#### Scenario: Foreign expired revoked or replayed ticket
+- **WHEN** a ticket is altered, expires, targets another job/artifact, or its owner/source access is revoked
+- **THEN** delivery is denied without private path/content disclosure, including revocation during streaming
+
+### Requirement: Measured fail-closed availability
+
+PDF availability SHALL remain false until exact deployed renderer/runtime/profile evidence passes actual complete-PDF 1000/5000 workloads including composition and numerical external API-health observation. Local ARM64 feasibility MUST NOT stand in for production AMD64 acceptance. Existing legacy v1 consumers MUST retain compatible responses.
+
+#### Scenario: Snapshot-only or different-runtime evidence
+- **WHEN** only B2 snapshot evidence, mock evidence or another architecture/runtime measurement exists
+- **THEN** server PDF capability remains unavailable
+
+#### Scenario: Accepted complete pipeline
+- **WHEN** the exact deployed runtime passes complete source/physical/composer/ACL and same-profile load acceptance
+- **THEN** capability advertises the pinned renderer and direct private download while legacy response semantics remain compatible
